    "notes": "Interior species (Zoo 0.84.0). REFERENCE: furniture in a shut-up room under canvas drop cloths and old bed sheets -- the shape of what is underneath (a sideboard, an armchair, a sofa, a stacked pair, a table with its legs showing, a heap) is the only thing that differs from one to the next. Faceted cloth: a grid over the hidden top, a folded skirt that flares to a pooled hem and a turned hem edge. Geometry planned purely in core/drape_forms.py. BUILT (0.84.0, unbeveled): 352-360 tris at armchair and chest sizes, 540 at 2.0 x 0.9 x 0.85, 678 at 3.2 x 1.6 x 2.2 (the grid is capped at 12 x 10). BUDGET 1000: a shut-up room holds a half dozen sheets; the grid cap is what holds it, not the dims."
